Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus15: enable the Iris video codec

video-codec@aa00000 is disabled, so there is no hardware video decode
or encode. As on the Surface Pro 11 ("arm64: dts: qcom: x1-denali:
Enable IRIS video codec"), enable it with the Microsoft-signed
qcvss8380.mbn from the Windows driver store. It uses the same
qcom/x1e80100/microsoft/Romulus/ directory as the ADSP and CDSP
firmware already extracted on this machine.

Iris loads firmware on first open, not at probe, so a missing file
only makes the V4L2 devices fail to open.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
index e1b1b784b..e12c50dc9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
@@ -55,3 +55,14 @@
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The video codec needs Microsoft-signed firmware, qcvss8380.mbn from the
+ * Windows driver store, placed next to the other Romulus DSP firmware.
+ * It loads on first use; until then, opening the device fails.
+ */
+&iris {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/x1e80100/microsoft/Romulus/qcvss8380.mbn";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
